  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485 (PRO1-Mod), 9600 baud, 8 data bits, even parity, 1 stop bit by default; the baud rate can be lowered to 4800, 2400 or 1200 (the register matrix also lists 600 and 300), data bits, parity and stop bit cannot be changed. The default address is 1.",
    "All registers are holding registers. Addresses are the hexadecimal register addresses of the Register matrix, written as printed, address base 0. The manual's 'Datablocks' column gives the number of 16-bit registers (01 = one, 02 = two, 04 = four).",
    "Measured values and the S0 output rate are IEEE 754 float32 in ABCD order (the manual says Float - Big Endian), so byte and word order are big. The other values are marked 'signed' in the manual and are mapped to int16, int32 or int64 by their size.",
    "The manual does not give units for power and energy (the S0 rate is in pulses per kWh); no unit is set for power or energy here. Voltage, frequency and current are given as V, Hz and A.",
    "The T1 and T2 energy registers are marked n/a for the single-tariff PRO1-S in the manual's table.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "E",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
